  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The VUP program at end of three years will be assessed with reference to the proportion of households in the bottom two categories of extreme poverty (as identified by the Ubudehe process)</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2008-12-31" value="34.00" year="2008">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline figure calculated for 18 VUP pilot Sectors for which Ubudehe data are well analyzed.The original figure (28.7) wasobtained from the Ubudehe database, which encountered many problems, which affected the original calculations.  Also, the revised34 percent figure was collected for households still in the Umudugudu (village) in 2009, and thus for a 2007-2009 change, itprovides a panel of households, which is more accurate. (See also CLSC-3 Program Document, p.41).</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2008-12-31"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2011-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="28.70">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The exact indicator value as shown in Board approved operation is &quot;&lt;28.70&quot; [less than 28.70], which was the initial proportion ofextremely poor households in the original reference baseline sample.  That implied that the operation would meet its goal if thecorresponding proportion of households in extreme poverty fell below 28.7 percent by the end of the operation.  Given the revisedbaseline figure, the equivalent revised target level  would be less than 30.00 percent.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="30.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Figure calculated for 18 VUP pilot Sectors for which Ubudehe data are well analyzed.  (See also CLSC-3 Program Document, p.41).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
